      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't care whether or not an avatar has that built-in in the form of actions, as it's still far inferior to actual tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-05T22:19:04.291Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As someone who's VR isn't working, it's a lot harder to play on desktop, because I cant point or hug my friends. It would be really nice if there was an option in the Action Menu that gave desktop users the ability to move their arms, there could be three options, 'Left Arm', 'Right Arm' and 'Both Arms'. This is a feature that avatar creators have added to a select few of their avatars, but a lot of desktop users don't have access to those avatars, or want to use their current avatar. So this would make the game a lot more easy and enjoyable for desktop users. I get that some avatars have idle animations and stuff like that, but the option to move your arms could have a toggle, so you can turn it on and off in the same menu.",
